  "ruleSetPolicy": "",
  "description": "The Spam Detection & Filtering System analyzes incoming messages (emails, SMS, or chat) to determine whether they are spam, suspicious, or legitimate. The system uses predefined criteria to prevent malicious or irrelevant messages from reaching users while ensuring important messages are not incorrectly marked as spam.\n\nThe system evaluates five critical factors:\n\nSender Reputation – Checks if the sender is known, unknown, or blacklisted.\nMessage Content – Analyzes keywords, links, and tone (e.g., promotional, phishing, normal).\nAttachments/Links – Determines if the message contains suspicious links or harmful attachments.\nUser Interaction History – Evaluates past interactions with the sender (e.g., frequent contact, first-time sender).\nEmail Authentication – Checks if the message passes standard email security checks.\n\nThe filtering decisions include Allow (Inbox), Mark as Suspicious (Spam Folder), or Block (Reject).",
